{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Abraham rose early in the morning.</b> Abraham's reason was because the verse says (Leviticus 7:38) ״בְּיוֹם צַוֹּתוֹ וגו׳ לְהַקְרִיב״ and so forth, and they of blessed memory said (Zevachim 98a) that one may not offer sacrifices at night, and therefore he went at a time that is fit for offering sacrifices, so that if the place should present itself to him he would not lack the time. And although the prophecy too was by day and he had no reason to delay until the next day — perhaps there was not enough time on that day to prepare and to travel to the place that HaShem had told him, and also to speak to Sarah along the way so that she would not notice the matter — and not out of negligence, heaven forbid. And the proof is ״וַיַּשְׁכֵּם אַבְרָהָם בַּבֹּקֶר״."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:42.098296854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}